## 3. Glassmorphism & Effects

The system uses three distinct glass styles to create depth without clutter.

### A. Standard Glass (`.glass`)
Used for: Main headers, standard cards, control bars.
```css
background: rgba(17, 29, 51, 0.4);
backdrop-filter: blur(16px);
border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15); /* Top highlight for 3D effect */
box-shadow: 0 4px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
B. Active Glass (.glass-lime)
Used for: Featured cards, active states, call-to-action areas.
code
CSS
background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(205, 222, 0, 0.1) 0%, rgba(17, 29, 51, 0.1) 100%);
backdrop-filter: blur(20px);
border: 1px solid rgba(205, 222, 0, 0.3);
box-shadow: 0 0 40px rgba(205, 222, 0, 0.1); /* Glow effect */
C. The "Cosmic" Background System
The application background is not a single color. It is a composed stack:
Layer 1: Radial Gradient (Deep Navy Center #0f172a → Void Black Edge #020408).
Layer 2: Animated colored "blobs" (Lime, Blue, Purple) moving slowly behind the UI.
Layer 3: Noise Texture SVG (opacity: 0.03) to prevent banding and add grit.
Layer 4: Vignette Overlay (radial-gradient(transparent 40%, #020408 100%)) to focus the center.
4. UI Components
Buttons
Primary: bg-rh-lime text-rh-primary font-bold shadow-lg shadow-rh-lime/20
Ghost/Nav: Pill-shaped, transparent background. Active state uses bg-rh-lime text-rh-primary.
Glass: Used for quick actions. hover:translate-x animations on icons.
Gradient Bars (Data Viz)
Do not use flat colors for progress bars. Use the Neon Flow style.
Structure: Pill-shaped container.
Gradient: Starts Pure White (#ffffff) and transitions to the Target Color (e.g., #CDDE00).
Glow: The bar must cast a colored shadow matching the target color (e.g., shadow-[0_0_14px_rgba(205,222,0,0.6)]).
Cards
Border Radius: rounded-2xl (16px) or rounded-3xl (24px) for large panels.
Interaction: hover:-translate-y-1 transition for clickable cards.
